            "review_text": "roman r\nRoubaix, France4 contributions\n0\nGood restaurant!\nJan 2016 • Family\nGood quality Vietnamese food at a fair price. Good ambience.I generally liked everything i had there though\n-Shaken beef: delicious!!! The beef was so tender and full of flavors. Came with a lot of onions which was so delicious and gave a right crunch to the dish. A little pricier than other dishes but so good. Recommended.\n-Pork Bahn MI: so much pork and it's not fatty. I love Bahn mis in general and shallot's Bahn MI is delicious. Their Bread is good too! \n-Egg rolls: I appreciate how they don't fill up the egg rolls with a bunch of vermicelli and little meat like other places! It was packed with meat filling! However it tasted average for me.\nRead more\nWritten January 8, 2016",
